**Done**
1. **URL params:** `normaliseUrl` in `worker/src/util.ts` now also strips `api_key`, `apikey`, `secret`, `jwt` and `sessionid`. A new test in `worker/test/util.test.ts` uses mixed-case versions of these and expects only `q=ok` to remain.
2. **Blocklist:** `DEFAULT_BLOCKLIST` in `extension/lib/blocklist.js` now includes `notion.com` and `facebook.com/messages*`. Matching URLs for both were added to the blocked list in `extension/test/privacy.test.mjs`.
3. **D1 vector cap:**
   - `D1VectorStore.query` in `worker/src/store.ts` now runs `SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM chunk_vectors` first.
   - Above 3000 rows (the new exported constant `D1_VECTOR_MAX_ROWS`), it logs one `console.warn` per isolate and returns `[]` without loading any rows, so search uses full-text only.
   - The new `worker/test/store.test.ts` uses a fake DB to test both sides of the cap: normal ranking under it, and `[]` with no row load above it.
   - The README free-tier note now says: "above 3,000 chunks the D1 vector search is skipped and search uses full-text only."

**Skipped**
4. **`content.js` early return:** the settings are read asynchronously, so adding a check before the timers start would wrap the whole startup in a promise. It would also change behaviour. A tab that opened on a blocked page (for example `x.com/messages`) would never capture after the user navigates to an allowed page in the same tab. Un-pausing wouldn't resume capture in tabs that are already open either. `capture()` already checks pause and the blocklist before it extracts or sends anything.

